.TH EDID-EDITOR 1 2026-09-15 "EDID Editor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
edid\-editor \- inspect and edit EDID data of displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B edid\-editor
.RI [ option ...]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B EDID Editor
inspects and edits EDID, the data a display sends to describe itself: its name, size,
timings, refresh ranges, color and HDR support, and audio formats.
It reads the EDID base block, CTA-861 extensions and DisplayID 1.x and 2.x blocks.
.PP
A
.I file
given opens at start.
Files ending in
.I .hex
or
.I .txt
are read as hexadecimal text, in the layouts printed by
.BR edid\-decode (1),
.B xrandr \-\-verbose
or Export Hex; other files are read as binary EDID.
Open from Display reads the EDID of a connected display from
.IR /sys/class/drm ;
the display itself is never written to.
.PP
An opened EDID starts on an overview of the display, which follows unsaved edits.
The sidebar lists the blocks and their groups, and the fields of the selected group are
shown with their plain names, units and descriptions.
Detailed timings open in a visual editor, where typing a refresh rate sets the pixel
clock.
CTA-861 and DisplayID data blocks can be added, duplicated, moved and deleted, two EDIDs
can be compared field by field, and Save recomputes the checksums.
.PP
.BR edid\-editor\-cli (1)
does the same from a terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Shows the options.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Shows all options, including those of the GTK application framework.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Save As.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Z ", " Ctrl+Shift+Z
Undo and Redo, for field edits and changes to groups.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search the groups; Escape clears the search.
.TP
.B Ctrl+?
Show the keyboard shortcuts.
.PP
While the group list has focus:
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Duplicate the group.
.TP
.B Delete
Delete the group.
.TP
.BR Alt+Up ", " Alt+Down
Move the group.
.TP
.BR Shift+F10 ", " Menu
Open the context menu.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/recently\-used.xbel
The files opened or saved recently, shared with other applications.
.TP
.I /sys/class/drm/*/edid
The EDID of connected displays, read by Open from Display.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR edid\-editor\-cli (1),
.BR edid\-decode (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/sachesi/edid\-editor/issues
.UE .
